  "scientific_review": [
    "All fifteen declared fixed-longitude sections and both January15/July15,2022 00Z dates remain as thirty original section/date cases. Exact cloud native components, coordinates, indices, hyperslabs, timestamps, missing support, selection scores/local peaks and selected5/10/20cm/s layers are retained, including unsuccessful or censored cases.",
    "Forty cloud tests passed in groups12/11/8/5/4. Frozen transverse v2 geometry, bounded exact-component transport, signed selection and connected-layer helpers are unchanged; actual sections are recomputed and audited in cloud. The ledger records failures/retries and reserves future first attempts. Counters are decoded/requested values, not wire traffic or scientific precision.",
    "All basin members use a fixed270degree true westward component, primary10cm/s, surface>5cm/s, complete finite native0–200m signed integral selection and first southern native tie. Selected gate/support-edge maxima stay unresolved without weaker interior substitution. Sensitivities share the selected column. No temperature/salinity gate is used.",
    "Atlantic31–35W/6.5–1.5S is a partial western central-SEC-context reach near Fernando de Noronha. Source Assuncao2023 distinguishes offshore cSEC/SEUC from coastal NBC/NBUC. Approximate source100m extent is regional context, not an imposed bottom or proof of branch identity. Northern/southern SEC branches and detached eddies are not target entities.",
    "Pacific100–140W/5.5–0.5S is a partial eastcentral SEC southern surface-branch reach. Johnson2002 describes eastern surface intensification, westward deepening and deep extensions, distinct from equatorial and subsurface countercurrents. An old142E northern-component150m reference is not transferred. Same-sign connected deep flow can mix features and does not independently identify a current bottom.",
    "Indian90–70E/15–10S is a partial southern zonal-mode SEC reach. Carr2026 describes zonal and northwest-meandering states. Northern meanders outside the declared gates are not captured by moving gates. Salinity fronts, SSH and20degree thermocline depths are different definitions. Original giant model packets were not downloaded or reproduced.",
    "All three basin owners remain separate from current:south-equatorial, whose family identity receives no inherited measurement. Exploratory gates and source connectors are not digitized current axes, full widths, route lengths or uncertainty bounds. Geographic maxima can be eddies or neighboring circulation; branch membership is not independently established.",
    "Native40-level0–5000m support and expected frame, dates, metadata and geometry are audited. Adjacent finite crossing brackets are required. Missing data, domain limits and bed depths censor rather than fill bottoms. A paired velocity-contour span is a model diagnostic rather than physical current thickness.",
    "All numerical field acquisition, retries, geometry, selection, contour calculations and tests ran sequentially in cloud on one idle CPU. Local work only prepared code, reviewed primary text/metadata, checked hashes and retained exact artifacts. Frozen helpers and file/inline/aggregate caps are preserved.",
    "Two instantaneous snapshots do not establish annual ranges, seasonal envelopes, independent observations or confidence bounds. Source retention leaves canonical depth registerv48, projection inventoryv12 and eddy baseline102size-referenced/34unresolved unchanged. No whole-route physical depth, matched area, volume, state passage or global sum is admitted. Subsequent projections must retain every original gate and gap."
